# Byte-exact checkouts on every OS. This repo's test corpus is ~360
# fixtures compared byte-for-byte (BOM handling, CRLF/bare-CR/bare-LF
# equivalence, malformed inputs, golden decode outputs) - any line-ending
# conversion on checkout silently corrupts them. Observed directly:
# GitHub's Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrote
# edge_brotli_english.expected's LF endings to CRLF and failed a
# byte-exact decode test that passes everywhere else. Side benefit:
# install.sh keeps its LF endings on Windows checkouts too.
* -text
